benevolence	noun [Latin benevolentia, of bene, well and volo, to will or wish. See Will.]1. The disposition to do good; good will; kindness; charitableness; the love, of mankind, accompanied with a desire to promote their happiness.The benevolence of God is one of his moral attributes; that attribute which delights in the happiness of intelligent beings. 'God is love.' 1 John 4:1.2. An act of kindness; good done; charity given.3. A species of contribution or tax illegally exacted by arbitrary kings of England.
