blasphemies	noun An indignity offered to God by words or writing; reproachful, contemptuous or irreverent words uttered impiously against Jehovah.Blasphemy is an injury offered to God, by denying that which is due and belonging to him, or attributing to him that which is not agreeable to his nature.In the middle ages, blasphemy was used to denote simply the blaming or condemning of a person or thing. Among the Greeks, to blaspheme was to use words of ill omen, which they were careful to avoid.1. That which derogates from the prerogatives of God. Mark 2:1.
blaspheming	participle present tense Uttering impious or reproachful words concerning God.
blasphemous	adjective Containing blasphemy; calumnious; impiously irreverent or reproachful towards God.
blasphemously	adverb Impiously; with impious irreverence to God.
