description	noun1. The act of delineating, or representing the figure of any thing by a plan, to be presented to the eye.2. The figure or appearance of any thing delineated, or represented by visible lines, marks, colors, etc.; as the description of a country, or of Solomons temple.3. The act of representing a thing by words or by signs, or the passage containing such representation; a representation of names, nature of properties, that gives to another a view of the thing. Homer abounds with beautiful and striking descriptions.4. A definition. All definitions must be less perfect descriptions of a material thing, than a visible figure or delineation.5. The qualities expressed in a representation; as, a man of this description Hence,6. The persons having the qualities expressed; a class of persons to whom a description is applicable, or who are in a similar condition.The secretary proceeds to examine, whether a difference ought to be permitted to remain between them and another description of public creditors.Persons of different descriptions.
descry	verb transitive1. To espy; to explore; to examine by observation.The house of Joseph sent to descry Bethel. Judges 1:23.2. To detect; to find out; to discover any thing concealed.3. To see; to behold; to have a sight of from a distance; as, the seamen descried land.4. To give notice of something suddenly discovered.DESCRY, noun Discovery; thing descovered.
