un A brood; as an eye of pheasants.EYE, verb transitive To fix the eye on; to look on; to view; to observe; particularly, to observe or watch narrowly, or with fixed attention.EYE nature's walks, shoot folly as it flies.EYE, verb intransitive To appear; to have an appearance.
