kerchiefs	noun [contracted from coverchief.]1. A head dress; a cloth to cover the head.2. A cloth used in dress.The word is now seldom used, except in its compound, handkerchief, and sometimes neckerchief.
kernels	noun1. The edible substance contained in the shell of a nut.2. Any thing included in a shell, husk or integument; a grain or corn; as a kernel of wheat or oats.3. The seed of pulpy fruit; as the kernel of an apple.4. The central part of any thing; a small mass around which other matter is concreted; a nucleus.5. A hard concretion in the flesh.KERN'EL, verb intransitive To harden or ripen into kernels; as the seeds of plants.
