laud	noun [Latin laus, laudis; Gr. ; Eng. loud. See Loud.]1. Praise; commendation; an extolling in words; honorable mention. [Little used.]2. That part of divine worship which consists in praise.3. Music or singing in honor of any one.LAUD, verb transitive [Latin laudo.] To praise in words alone, or with words and singing; to celebrate.
