nuts	noun [It seems to be allied to knot, a bunch or hard lump.]1. The fruit of certain trees and shrubs, consisting of a hard shell inclosing a kernel. A nut is properly the pericarp of the fruit. Various kinds of nuts are distinguished; as walnut, chestnut, hazlenut, butternut.2. In mechanics, a small cylinder or other body, with teeth or projections corresponding with the teeth or grooves of a wheel.3. The projection near the eye of an anchor.NUT, verb transitive To gather nuts.
