oppositions	noun [Latin oppositio.]1. Situation so as to front something else; a standing over against; as the opposition of two mountains or buildings.2. The act of opposing; attempt to check, restrain or defeat. he makes opposition to the measure; the bill passed without opposition Will any opposition be made to the suit, to the claim or demand?3. Obstacle. the river meets with no opposition in its course to the ocean.4. Resistance; as the opposition of enemies. Virtue will break through all opposition5. Contrariety; repugnance in principle; as the opposition of the heart to the laws of God.6. Contrariety of interests, measures on designs. The two parties are in opposition to each other.7. Contrariety or diversity of meaning; as one term used in opposition to another.8. Contradiction; inconsistency.9. The collective body of opposers; in England, the party in Parliament which opposed the ministry; in America, the party that opposed the existing administration.10. In astronomy, the situation of two heavenly bodies, when distant from each other 180 degrees.
