our	adjective1. Pertaining or belonging to us; as our country; our rights; our troops.2. Ours, which is primarily the possessive case of our is never used as an adjective, but as a substitute for the adjective and the noun to which it belongs. Your house is on a plain; ours is on a hill. This is good English, but certainly ours must be the nominative to is, or it has none.Their organs are better disposed than ours for receiving grateful impressions from sensible objects.Here ours stands in the place of our organs, and cannot, in conformity with any rule of construction, be in the possessive case.The same thing was done by them in suing in their courts, which is now done by us in suing in ours.
