pollux	noun A fixed star of the second magnitude, in the constellation Gemini or the Twins.1. [See Castor.]
pomegranate	noun [Latin pomum, an apple, and granatum, grained. See Grain and Granate.]1. The fruit of a tree belonging to the genus Punica. This fruit is as large as an orange, having a hard rind filled with a soft pulp and numerous seeds. It is of a reddish color.2. The tree that produces pomegranates.3. An ornament resembling a pomegranate on the robe and ephod of the Jewish high priest.
