rejoice	verb intransitive rejois'.To experience joy and gladness in a high degree; to be exhilarated with lively and pleasurable sensations; to exult.When the righteous are in authority, the people rejoice; but when the wicked beareth rule, the people mourn. Proverbs 29:2.I will rejoice in thy salvation. Psalms 9:14.REJOICE, verb transitive rejois'. To make joyful; to gladden; to animate with lively pleasurable sensations; to exhilarate.Whoso loveth wisdom rejoiceth his father. Proverbs 29:3.While she, great saint, rejoices heaven.
