reveal	verb transitive [Latin revelo; re and velo, to veil.]1. To disclose; to discover; to show; to make known something before unknown or concealed; as, to reveal secrets.2. To disclose, discover or make known from heaven. God has been pleased to reveal his will to man.The wrath of God is revealed from heaven against all ungodliness and unrighteousness of men. Romans 1:17.REVE'AL, noun A revealing; disclosure. [Not in use.]
