saffron	noun [The radical sense is to fail, or to be hollow, or to be exhausted.1. A plant of the genus Crocus. The bastard saffron is of the genus Carthamus, and the meadow saffron of the genus Colchicum.2. In the materia medica, saffron is formed of the stigmata of the Crocus officinalis, dried on a kiln and pressed into cakes.SAF'FRON, adjective Having the color of saffron flowers; yellow; as a saffron face; a saffron streamer.SAF'FRON, verb transitive To tinge with saffron; to make yellow; to gild.
