stedfast	STEDFAST adjective [stead and fast.]1. Fast fixed; firm; firmly fixed or established; as the STEDFAST globe of earth.2. Constant; firm; resolute; not fickle or wavering.Abide STEDFAST to thy neighbor in the time of his trouble.Whom resist stedfast in the faith. 1 Peter 5:9.3. Steady; as STEDFAST sight.
