tithe	noun The tenth part of any thing; but appropriately, the tenth part of the increase annually arising from the profits of land and stock, allotted to the clergy for their support. Tithes are personal, predial, or mixed; personal, when accruing from labor, art, trade and navigation; predial, when issuing from the earth, as hay, wood and fruit; and mixed, when accruing from beasts, which are fed from the ground.TITHE, verb transitive To levy a tenth part on; to tax to the amount of a tenth.When thou hast made an end of tithing all the tithes of thine increase. Deuteronomy 26:12.Ye tithe mint and rue. Luke 11:42.TITHE, verb intransitive To pay tithes.
