voyage	noun1. A passing by sea or water from one place, port or country to another, especially a passing or journey by water to a distant place or country. Captain Latin made more than a hundred voyages to the West Indies. A voyage over lake Superior is like a voyage to Bermuda.2. The practice of traveling. [Not in use.]VOYAGE, verb intransitive To sail or pass by water.VOYAGE, verb transitive To travel; to pass over.I with pain Voyagd th unreal, vast, unbounded deep.
vulture	noun A genus of fowls, belonging to the order of Accipiters. The bill is straight, but hooked at the end, and covered at the base by a cere of skin. The head is naked. There are thirteen species, all carnivorous and rapacious. The vultur is one of the largest kinds of fowls, and the Condor of South America, one of this family, is the largest species of flying animals that has been discovered.
